WEBVTT
NOTE SYNC_TYPE: HUMAN_VERIFIED
NOTE Track: 1-03 - The Brass Escapement
NOTE Artist: Fractured Prisms
NOTE Album: 1984: 1883 (The Rock Opera)

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.500
Patch the cables into the rack

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:33.000
Wind the mainspring and turn it back

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.500
A mathematical lullaby

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:44.000
Underneath a clockwork sky

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.500
If I keep the tempo locked in place

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:55.000
Time cannot touch my sister's face

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.500
Tick-tock goes the brass escapement

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:08.500
Down in the synthesizer basement

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Hold the pendulum, freeze the gear!

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Keep the twentieth century out of here!

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:28.000
The machine is cold, the voltage is high

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:34.000
Teaching the oscillators how to cry!

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Count every beat, measure the breath

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:47.000
Building a clock that outruns death!

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:11.000
He promised her forever in a church in town

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:17.000
Then broke the vow when the sun went down

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:23.000
They call it a burden, I call it grace

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:29.000
To be the anchor in this quiet place

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:35.000
It isn't a tragedy, it's just Tuesday night

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:42.000
Keeping the lanterns burning bright

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:12.000
Silver flute over silicon wire

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:18.000
Victorian coal in an electric fire

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:24.000
Two halves of a single beating heart

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:31.000
Never to be torn apart!

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:51.000
Hold the pendulum, freeze the gear!

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:57.000
Keep the twentieth century out of here!

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:03.000
Count every beat, measure the breath

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:10.000
Building a clock that outruns death!

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:28.000
Tick-tock... eighteen eighty-three...

